    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug! The issue was that the main `frai` program had a global `--ci` option definition (line 605) that was consuming the `--ci` flag before it could be passed to the `gate` subcommand.\n\n**The fix:**\n- Removed the `.option('--ci', ...)` from the main program's option definitions\n- Set `ci: false` in the default action handler (since the subcommands that need `--ci` already define their own options)\n- Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n\n**Verification:**\nRunning `frai gate init --ci` in an empty directory now correctly creates both:\n- \u2705 `FRAI-SPEC.md`  \n- \u2705 `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n\nThe `--ci` flag is now properly passed through to the `frai-gate` CLI without being consumed by the main program.",
